        {
          "id": "p10-3-1",
          "panel": 3,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "款どうし、項どうしは、原則動かせねえ!",
          "en": "Can't move money between the big categories!",
          "note": "Real rule: a Japanese city's budget is split by the council into “kan” and “kō” categories, and money can't be moved between them (Local Autonomy Act, Art. 220(2)). Smaller moves still need the city's formal procedure."
